@championswimmer Fair critique on naming! "`quick`/`standard`/`advanced`" describes _speed/capability intent_ rather than model size.

I went with `quick`/`standard`/`advanced` because it maps to _task complexity_ rather than model characteristics. The LLM decides _"this task needs advanced reasoning"_ not _"this task needs a large model."_

Open to changing the enum values if maintainers prefer different naming. @adamdotdevin thoughts?

@repolevedavaj 

Did you ever hear back?

I'm looking to setup auth for OpenCode to GitHub Copilot using only an API token as well.

I honestly much rather have the option to toggle YOLO within the session, without having to exit. gemini-cli Ctrl+Y or Shirt+Tab (auto-accept edits).

If you want to follow @orangeswim suggestion, here you have. Use responsibly.
```sh
﻿cat >> ~/.config/opencode/opencode-yolo.json << 'EOF'
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "*": {
      "*": "allow"
    }
  }
}
EOF

alias oc-yolo='OPENCODE_CONFIG=~/.config/opencode/opencode-yolo.json opencode'
```
